Changes to packages/core/src/memory/arcSummary.ts:

1. Update the system prompt array — add this line BEFORE the existing final 'in-world chronicle' instruction:

  'A campaign bible of established world facts, NPCs, factions, and open threads is provided before the recaps; reference its entries canonically.',

2. Update the import block:

  import type { CampaignBibleInput, SessionRecapRecord } from './summary.js';
  import { MemorySummaryError } from './summary.js';

3. Update the ComposeArcSummaryInput interface:

  export interface ComposeArcSummaryInput {
    campaignId: string;
    arcId: string;
    recaps: SessionRecapRecord[];
    bible: CampaignBibleInput;
  }

4. Replace `const userContent = renderRecaps(input.recaps);` with:

  const userContent = renderBibleAndRecaps(input.bible, input.recaps);

5. Add these helpers (place after renderRecaps):

  function renderBibleAndRecaps(
    bible: CampaignBibleInput,
    recaps: SessionRecapRecord[],
  ): string {
    return [renderBible(bible), renderRecaps(recaps)].join('\n\n');
  }

  function renderBible(bible: CampaignBibleInput): string {
    const sections: Array<readonly [string, readonly string[]]> = [
      ['worldFacts', bible.worldFacts],
      ['majorNpcs', bible.majorNpcs],
      ['factions', bible.factions],
      ['openThreads', bible.openThreads],
    ];
    const blocks = sections.map(([name, items]) => {
      const body =
        items.length === 0 ? '(none)' : items.map((s) => '- ' + s).join('\n');
      return '### ' + name + '\n' + body;
    });
    return ['## campaign bible', ...blocks].join('\n');
  }

Changes to packages/core/test/arcSummary.test.ts:

1. Add these constants near the top (after the helpers, before the describe):

  const EMPTY_BIBLE = {
    worldFacts: [],
    majorNpcs: [],
    factions: [],
    openThreads: [],
  };

  const NON_EMPTY_BIBLE = {
    worldFacts: ['Emberfall sits on a fault line'],
    majorNpcs: ['Mira the runesmith'],
    factions: ['Lantern Court'],
    openThreads: ['The chalk sigil is unsolved'],
  };

2. Pass `bible: EMPTY_BIBLE` to each of the four existing tests. For the prompt-rendering happy-path test (currently 'renders each session recap and stateDelta into the user prompt'), use NON_EMPTY_BIBLE instead and ADD an assertion that the bible content appears (see new test below — you can fold the bible assertion into the existing test if neater).

3. Add this new test inside the existing describe('composeArcSummary'):

  it('renders the campaign bible into the user prompt', async () => {
    let captured: ModelCompleteInput | undefined;
    const model = fakeModel((input) => {
      captured = input;
      return 'OK';
    });
    await composeArcSummary(model, {
      campaignId: 'camp-1',
      arcId: 'arc-1',
      recaps: [recap('session-1', 'Mira found the chalk sigil.', '2026-05-20T10:00:00.000Z')],
      bible: NON_EMPTY_BIBLE,
    });
    const userContent = captured?.messages[0].content ?? '';
    expect(userContent).toContain('campaign bible');
    expect(userContent).toContain('Emberfall sits on a fault line');
    expect(userContent).toContain('Mira the runesmith');
    expect(userContent).toContain('Lantern Court');
    expect(userContent).toContain('The chalk sigil is unsolved');
  });

Changes to packages/cli/src/play.ts:

In rollupCampaignArc, the existing call to composeArcSummary becomes:

  summary = await composeArcSummary(deps.model, {
    campaignId,
    arcId: CAMPAIGN_ARC_ID,
    recaps,
    bible: { worldFacts: [], majorNpcs: [], factions: [], openThreads: [] },
  });

This empty-bible literal is a temporary placeholder. T4 replaces it with the result of extractBibleWithRetry. Do not generalize or extract a constant — T4 will remove it entirely.

NOTE TO IMPLEMENTER: After this commit, the arc summary will be model-authored but will not yet reference any bible (the empty placeholder produces empty bullet lists in the user prompt). That is fine — T4 wires the real extraction. The point of this task is to make composeArcSummary capable of consuming a bible without yet supplying one from the model.
